  --hash=sha256:d920abdfa61279ba1a2ef9484aab07bf03331f8c08a10120fa332353d06e6932 \\\n    --hash=sha256:da2af0d7aebfc2074080d72efa6ab8317c62481ef1f896f65d9999c1c01f4494 \\\n    --hash=sha256:dd8ea6ebee7aedbf7c749fa80521d9ccf1ba473e0d1e14805caafbaad281c889 \\\n    --hash=sha256:de8b364c423ef0a4bad9069657d617f9a5d2b2062457a89b1fa16ee199c399c1 \\\n    --hash=sha256:df1ae86ff54725a01fa1a0510b914ca53a161b7050be74f6204e24aded5971d0 \\\n    --hash=sha256:dff05cb7016dff1e9fd68f4122c127b65dfc59de5306cfb7ad92f956f230bee2 \\\n    --hash=sha256:e1a622f13970d81f95d0c72f9dc090dce9085fccfa4c9f2174377ee32bd15786 \\\n    --hash=sha256:e49fb0d1ce92cfa0cb198cc5b1b11cdf9d0638658e2a2db2687e39db7c87fc78 \\\n    --hash=sha256:e5c802729725bd07e2bc3ab7b76dc7e0bbfc53129d8f1eb1c002c24cf774717e \\\n    --hash=sha256:e841068dc0be4cb6dfb5c890eb88cbdcff2f4a332393c7ec94e8e618bd32c1a8 \\\n    --hash=sha256:e916035e3e9930cbdfdd10abf48861340221857f45509565898e012263f7b289 \\\n    --hash=sha256:eba154571c16e032112afac0dc2dfe9e63c2ceb7aedd07bb7eecf2ce26d4dd4c \\\n    --hash=sha256:f03460ff076f70ab595bb45a0205ccea1971443575b6920c52e755dec2b3fbfe \\\n    --hash=sha256:f0ec3b750b59375eab5b0fb2b9254810c00a3375be6d789899f1055a1d556237 \\\n    --hash=sha256:f291bcf42ae98eb5107edb162c3c998b4a89648fd8e99ed4cbd12705292788cd \\\n    --hash=sha256:f61efe1d2fe0de16158a5fe1d1cf3c14bdb6aecd54d8938fd26512c525c1f624 \\\n    --hash=sha256:f68edfc67aabac33708941f26f22a7b8e9f81429bc0cf249fcf7d66b23af8d19 \\\n    --hash=sha256:fa95848c929b6a75f6848d3c9793e59db365ee436776e57db835cdbfa79ba977 \\\n    --hash=sha256:fd9f8797427910198f95bced71ddfed61130d7e349213bfb8466c9c99e2c46a8 \\\n    --hash=sha256:fdb4ca07ab75ffadab4a8b135ad59cdbb3156b99310f3d565370da74a15d6bd3\nwerkzeug==3.1.9 \\\n    --hash=sha256:55ca7c70a75689be937aa27f8ff4b018f06ff4838fc73045560bf0f5a1291060 \\\n    --hash=sha256:6392e50c78460ba618e5b21f08a71f59c99ce99cdc6cf6e3dd7e6ccca8754fab\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nlock = Path('backend/requirements.lock').read_text()\nentries=[];cur=None\nfor raw in lock.splitlines():\n    line=raw.rstrip()\n    if not line or line.lstrip().startswith('#'): continue\n    if line[:1] in (' ','\\t'):\n        if cur is not None: cur.append(line)\n        continue\n    if cur is not None: entries.append(cur)\n    cur=[line]\nif cur: entries.append(cur)\n# direct deps first, then the rest\norder={'flask':0,'gunicorn':1}\nentries.sort(key=lambda e: order.get(e[0].split('==')[0], 2))\ntext='\\n'.join('\\n'.join(e) for e in entries)+'\\n'\nPath('backend/requirements.txt').write_text(text)\nprint(text)\n\"","time":{"start":1794359292114,"end":1794359292216}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c825f0ca001EBGT5Y0vsP1Gv5","sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","messageID":"msg_1c824d42e001V7hwODYp2U7cnn"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794359292506,"sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","part":{"id":"prt_1c825f13c001wMtNAza3D1ZXWW","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c824d42e001V7hwODYp2U7cnn","sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":96937,"input":1043,"output":232,"reasoning":1518,"cache":{"write":0,"read":94144}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794359335244,"sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","part":{"id":"prt_1c82698e9001LgeC6SDqBvdG0f","messageID":"msg_1c825f1fa001YRg1qbdhUxRERe","sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794359335244,"sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","part":{"id":"prt_1c82698f4001D7EiYZv8P2jyDV","messageID":"msg_1c825f1fa001YRg1qbdhUxRERe","sessionID":"ses_e37f9f7ebffegqor2mGm8Awaxt","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build a shared Kanban board app: Flask JSON API under `/api` (auth + tasks, SQLite in `./data`) with a React/TypeScript + Tailwind + Vite frontend served by the backend on port 8000, per the spec (columns `todo`/`in_progress`/`done`, 1-based contiguous positions, drag-and-drop, dialogs with API validation messages).\n- Build from the existing minimal scaffold (`backend/app.py`, `frontend/`, `Dockerfile`, `README.md`) without breaking the documented install/run contract.\n\n## Important Details\n- Backend: `backend/app.py` entry, `flask==3.1.3` + `gunicorn==26.2.0` only (hashes pinned in `backend/requirements.lock`, used as pip constraints); no new backend deps allowed ideally.\n- Frontend: React 19.3.1, Vite 8.3.5, Tailwind CSS v4.3.5 via `@tailwindcss/vite`; `npm ci` + `npm run build` → `frontend/dist`; deps must stay pinned exactly in `package.json` + `package-lock.json`.\n- Auth: register 201, login 200 `{\"token\": ...}` (body kept token-only; extra `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` added), `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, 401 with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer` for write ops; reads (`GET /api/tasks`, `GET /api/tasks/{id}`) are public.\n- Error format: `{\"error\": \"...\", \"errors\": [...]}` (400 validation, 404 `Task not found`, 409 `Username already exists`, 401 `Invalid username or password` / `Authentication required`).\n- `counts` computed from the filtered set (self-consistent with `items`); `total = len(items)`; filters `status`/`priority` validated → 400 on invalid values.\n- PATCH: only given fields change; position clamped to column bounds; status change without position appends to end of target column; only the patched task's `updated_at` is touched.\n- Task fields: `id, title, description, status, priority, position, updated_at`; priorities `low|medium|high`; title required ≤200 chars, description ≤5000.\n- `updated_at` format: `datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")`.\n- DnD uses native HTML5 drag events (no extra deps); insertion index computed by pointer position over `[data-task-id]` cards; list-level handlers `stopPropagation` so section handler only handles padding/header drops.\n- Sandbox tool rules: avoid literal `/run/home/...` paths (use `$HOME/...` or `/tmp/venv/...`); avoid bare `/tmp/opencode` (must have a trailing path segment); no Docker available; no browser for UI testing.\n- Leftover test artifacts to clean: `/workspace/.server.log`, `backend/__pycache__/`, test DB at `/workspace/data/kanban.db` (git-excluded via `.git/info/exclude` line `/data/*.db`).\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Backend `backend/app.py` fully implemented and API-tested via curl: register/login/me/logout, task CRUD, ordering, contiguous renumbering on move/delete, filters, counts, validation messages, health endpoint, frontend catch-all (404 for unknown `/api/*` paths).\n- Verified edge cases: reorder within column, cross-column move, position clamping (`position:99` → end), invalid position/json → 400, unknown fields ignored, create appends, 404s, 401s.\n- Frontend deps installed: `tailwindcss@4.3.5`, `@tailwindcss/vite@4.3.5`, `@types/react@19.3.0`, `@types/react-dom@19.3.0` (pinned exact); `npm ci` and `npm run build` verified clean (dist: `index-HcS1gV9l.js`, `index-BUKqB2bt.css`).\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` passes (tsconfig strict, `src/vite-env.d.ts` added).\n- Served frontend verified via running gunicorn: `GET /` → 200 HTML, assets 200, Tailwind classes present in built CSS.\n\n### Active\n- Investigating whether `pip install -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock` (the Dockerfile command) fails: it errored with `ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements ... flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bc...` under pip 25.1.1.\n- Located the message at `$HOME/venv2/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/_internal/exceptions.py:527` and `require_hashes` logic in `pip/_internal/cli/req_command.py` (lines ~142, 266, 286: `options.require_hashes = True`), to determine what triggers require-hashes (constraints-with-hashes vs. config) and whether the Docker image's pip behaves the same.\n\n### Blocked\n- Unknown whether the given `Dockerfile` pip install step succeeds with the hash-bearing `requirements.lock` as constraints; cannot run Docker to confirm.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Read `pip/_internal/cli/req_command.py` around lines 260–290 to find the exact condition that sets `options.require_hashes = True`, then test fixes on copies of `requirements.txt`/`requirements.lock` in `/tmp/opencode/pipexp` (e.g., add hashes + full pins to `requirements.txt`, or strip hashes from the lock) using `$HOME/venv2/bin/pip install --dry-run -r ... -c ...`.\n2. Apply the chosen fix so the Dockerfile's install command works, stop/restart the local gunicorn, run a final end-to-end API + built-frontend smoke test, then remove `.server.log`, `backend/__pycache__/`, and `data/kanban.db`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: full Flask API (auth, tasks, SQLite at `Path.cwd()/data/kanban.db`, `init_db()` at import, frontend serving).\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`: fixed build contract — pip install with `-r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock`, `npm ci` + `npm run build`, gunicorn on 8000.\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.txt`, `/workspace/backend/requirements.lock`: pinned deps; lock contains hashes (cause of open pip issue).\n- `/workspace/frontend/package.json`, `/workspace/frontend/package-lock.json`: pinned devDeps (tailwind, @tailwindcss/vite, @types/react, @types/react-dom).\n- `/workspace/frontend/vite.config.ts`: react + tailwindcss plugins, `/api` proxy to `localhost:8000`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx`: board state, DnD drop index math (`handleDropAt`), auth/filter/dialog orchestration.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts`: fetch wrapper, `ApiError` (status + `errors[]`), token storage (`kanban_token`), task/auth calls.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/components/BoardColumn.tsx`: columns, cards, priority badges, drop indicator, list-level dragover/drop handlers.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/components/TaskDialog.tsx`, `AuthDialog.tsx`, `Modal.tsx`: dialogs showing API validation messages, two-step delete confirm.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/index.css`: `@import \"tailwindcss\";` (only CSS file).\n- `/workspace/frontend/tsconfig.json`, `/workspace/frontend/src/vite-env.d.ts`: typecheck config.","time":{"start":1794359335156,"end":1794359335160}}}
